The ability to make traps would provide a safer method of identifying
unknown wands.  If you are drastically going to increase the types of
traps, you are going to have to be very careful walking around.
Situation:
  Albert the A...... decides to play a joke on some future explorer.
He surrounds the staircase with traps of death before he croaks and
leaves (unlucky for someone) a dangerous bones level.
  Personally, I would rather stick with my pickaxe making trapdoors.
This allows you to make one of the more useful trapdoors, and takes
a respectable amount of effort (so is less likely to be abused)
  Also, what would happen if you create a trap while floating over a
trap of some other variety?

